<title>FRANCE: AXA at all-time high on profit remarks.</title>
<headline>AXA at all-time high on profit remarks.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French insurer AXA-UAP hit an all time high on Wednesday as the company said it was &quot;at ease&quot; with analysts forecasts for 1996 net attributable profits of 3.6 to 3.9 billion francs.</p>
<p>At 1221 GMT, Axa was 1.11 percent higher at 382.20, below a high of 383.40 francs. The CAC-40 was up 1.69 percent at the tome.</p>
<p>In Axa's stock market history, going back to 1985, the company has never seen its shares so high. Axa merged with UAP late last year.</p>
</text>
